        <mxCell id="note" value="BN = BitNet b1.58 2B4T (I2_S). Q4, Q8, F16 = Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct at Q4_K_M, Q8_0, and FP16.&lt;br&gt;Common four-thread operating point, mean of five repeats; disk and peak RAM are single measurements.&lt;br&gt;In the scatter, BitNet and the k-quant sit on the Pareto frontier together; Q8_0 and FP16 are dominated on both axes." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=9;fontColor=#52514e;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20.0" y="592.0" width="1220.0" height="46.0" as="geometry" />
